/-! ## Tier 3 Phase W.8 — `msm_gamma_N` Fiat–Shamir composition
    + scalar algebraic-identity goldens

Each `gamma1`/`gamma2` row reproduces the CA sigma-proof FS
challenge pipeline
  `γ_N(ρ, i[, j]) := scalarToBytes (scalarUniformFrom64Bytes
                         (sha2_512 (scalarToBytes ρ ++ [i [, j]])))`.
The VM-side companion invokes the matching primitives
(`scalar_to_bytes` ∘ `ByteArray.push` ∘ `new_scalar_from_sha2_512`)
and compares to the same hex literal — a full composed pipeline
cross-engine binding covering the exact byte sequence feeding every
sigma-proof's Fiat–Shamir transcript.

The scalar-identity rows pin LHS and RHS of an algebraic identity
(e.g. `(a+b)c = ac + bc`) to the SAME hex literal on BOTH engines:
this catches a `scalar_add` ↔ `scalar_mul` swap or `scalar_sub` sign
flip that the per-op W.6 rows could miss, because the single-op rows
only verify each op in isolation, not the compositional identities
that downstream proof logic depends on. -/

/-- Helper: Lean-side `msm_gamma_1` byte-pipeline. -/
private def gamma1Bytes (rho : RistrettoScalar) (i : UInt8) : ByteArray :=
  let input := (scalarToBytes rho).push i
  match scalarUniformFrom64Bytes (sha2_512 input) with
  | some r => scalarToBytes r
  | none   => ByteArray.empty

/-- Helper: Lean-side `msm_gamma_2` byte-pipeline. -/
private def gamma2Bytes (rho : RistrettoScalar) (i j : UInt8) : ByteArray :=
  let input := ((scalarToBytes rho).push i).push j
  match scalarUniformFrom64Bytes (sha2_512 input) with
  | some r => scalarToBytes r
  | none   => ByteArray.empty

/-- Lean-side `γ₁(ρ=42, i=0)` — computed independently via
`scalarToBytes ∘ scalarUniformFrom64Bytes ∘ sha2_512` of the pushed
byte buffer. -/
