/-! ## Tier 3 Phase W.9 — Inversion / multiplicative identity goldens
    + `prepend_domain_context` byte-layout goldens

**Inversion identities.** Each row pins a 32-byte hex obtained from
`scalarToBytes` applied to an algebraic expression over
`RistrettoScalar = ZMod ℓ`. The matching VM row reproduces the same
bytes via `ristretto255::scalar_{add,sub,mul,neg,invert}` natives on
`curve25519-dalek`. For LHS/RHS-pair rows the Move VM independently
computes the LHS factored form and RHS factored form and requires
BOTH to equal the same hex literal — the identity then holds
byte-for-byte on the VM.

**`prepend_domain_context` identities.** Each row pins the exact byte
layout `[chain_id] ++ bcs(sender) ++ bcs(contract) ++ body` used at
the top of every CA sigma-proof Fiat–Shamir transcript. The Move
side reconstructs it via `std::bcs::to_bytes` + `vector::append`;
the Lean side computes via `SigmaVerifiers.prependDomainContext` on
`Address32` (which holds the 32-byte BCS encoding verbatim). -/

/-- `(7⁻¹)⁻¹ = 7`. Double inversion is identity on `ℤ/ℓℤ^*`. -/
example : scalarToBytes ((s 7)⁻¹⁻¹) = scalarToBytes (s 7) := by
  native_decide

/-- `(42⁻¹)⁻¹ = 42`. -/
example : scalarToBytes ((s 42)⁻¹⁻¹) = scalarToBytes (s 42) := by
  native_decide

/-- `(1001⁻¹)⁻¹ = 1001 = 0x3e9`. -/
