/-! ## Tier 3 Phase W.12 — Fiat–Shamir CHALLENGE SCALAR cross-engine binding

Phases W.10 + W.11 bind the **byte-level** SHA-512 digest of the FS
prefix on 8 (fixture × variant) axes. But the operationally critical
value — the ACTUAL sigma challenge scalar consumed by every verifier's
MSM equation — is the reduction of that 64-byte digest modulo ℓ
(Ristretto subgroup order), serialized as 32 little-endian bytes.
The composition is `scalarToBytes ((scalarUniformFrom64Bytes (sha2_512
prefix)).getD 0)` on Lean side and `scalar_to_bytes(&new_scalar_from_
sha2_512(prefix))` on VM side.

Phase W.5 pinned this pipeline on RAW strings (`""`, `"abc"`,
`"movement"`, `DST-as-input`). W.12 pins it on the FULL FS prefix byte
sequences — catching a regression that (i) affects the scalar reduction
only for prefix-shaped (>64 B) inputs with specific byte distributions,
or (ii) modifies either engine's hash-to-scalar path in a way that
cancels perfectly on W.5's short inputs but diverges on W.10/W.11's
multi-hundred-byte prefixes. -/

/-- Lean-side FS-challenge-scalar computation: hash → reduce → serialize. -/
private def fsChallengeBytes (msg : ByteArray) : ByteArray :=
  match scalarUniformFrom64Bytes (sha2_512 msg) with
  | some s => scalarToBytes s
  | none => ByteArray.empty

/-- Every challenge scalar is 32 bytes (LE, mod ℓ). -/
example : (fsChallengeBytes ByteArray.empty).size = 32 := by native_decide

