/-! ## Tier 3 Phase W.17 — full FS-MESSAGE axis (prefix || X-point bytes)

Background: All W.10-W.16 bindings stop at the FS PREFIX. The actual
sigma challenge is
  `new_scalar_from_sha2_512(prefix || compress(X_0) || ... || compress(X_n))`.
The byte-level concatenation of compressed X-points onto the prefix,
and its propagation through SHA-512 + scalar reduction, has zero
cross-engine binding. A regression that (a) swaps the order of X-points
in the FS-message assembly; (b) appends X-bytes BEFORE the prefix
instead of after; (c) drops a trailing X-point silently; (d) uses a
different concatenation width (e.g. 16-byte instead of 32-byte
compressed Ristretto); or (e) re-hashes instead of single SHA-512 —
would pass every W.10-W.16 row unchanged.

W.17 circumvents the open `canonicalEncode` noncomputability problem
by using ALREADY-PINNED compressed Ristretto byte arrays (G and H
from `ristrettoBasepointBytes` / `confidentialAssetHashBaseBytes`) as
synthetic X-point bytes. This binds the FULL FS-message byte
concatenation + SHA-512 + scalar reduction path for 4 fixtures:
  * `wdMsgA` — prefix || G (1 X-point).
  * `wdMsgB` — prefix || G || H (2 X-points, canonical order).
  * `wdMsgC` — prefix || H || G (2 X-points, SWAPPED order — pins X-order).
  * `wdMsgD` — prefix || G||G||G||H||H||H (6 X-points; stresses longer
     arrays and repeated point bytes).
-/

/-- Withdrawal FS message = withdrawal FS prefix || n × compressed X bytes. -/
private def wdMsgA : ByteArray :=
  withdrawalFsPrefixBytes ++ ristrettoBasepointBytes
private def wdMsgB : ByteArray :=
  withdrawalFsPrefixBytes ++ ristrettoBasepointBytes ++ confidentialAssetHashBaseBytes
private def wdMsgC : ByteArray :=
  withdrawalFsPrefixBytes ++ confidentialAssetHashBaseBytes ++ ristrettoBasepointBytes
private def wdMsgD : ByteArray :=
  withdrawalFsPrefixBytes ++
  ristrettoBasepointBytes ++ ristrettoBasepointBytes ++ ristrettoBasepointBytes ++
  confidentialAssetHashBaseBytes ++ confidentialAssetHashBaseBytes ++ confidentialAssetHashBaseBytes

/-- Size pins: each message = 837-byte prefix + 32 × num_X_points. -/
example : wdMsgA.size = 869  := by native_decide  -- 837 +  32
example : wdMsgB.size = 901  := by native_decide  -- 837 +  64
example : wdMsgC.size = 901  := by native_decide
example : wdMsgD.size = 1029 := by native_decide  -- 837 + 192

