/-! ## Phase W.20 — transfer auditor-count × full FS-MESSAGE axis

W.13 binds the transfer FS PREFIX for {1, 2, 3, 2-swapped} auditor
variants. W.18 / W.19 bind the transfer full FS-MESSAGE only at 0
auditors. A regression that corrupts **only** the auditor-driven
X-point emission step of the FS message (e.g. drops the auditor
X-block but still propagates auditors into the prefix) slips
through W.13 (message-less) and through W.18/W.19 (auditorless).

Phase W.20 closes this seam: for each of the 4 W.13 prefixes
(`1A`, `2A`, `3A`, `2A_swapped`) we pin the full FS-message in
2 X-point shapes (A: `prefix ‖ G`, B: `prefix ‖ H ‖ G` — reversed
order, pins per-variant X-order) = 8 fixtures × 2 bindings = 16
new binding rows. Critical distinctness pins include
`tr2aMsgA ≠ tr2aSwapMsgA` (binds auditor-order propagation into
the full message) and `tr1aMsgA ≠ tr2aMsgA` (binds auditor-count
propagation).
-/

/-- 1-auditor transfer FS messages. -/
private def tr1aMsgA : ByteArray :=
  transferFsPrefixBytes1A ++ ristrettoBasepointBytes
private def tr1aMsgB : ByteArray :=
  transferFsPrefixBytes1A ++ confidentialAssetHashBaseBytes ++ ristrettoBasepointBytes

/-- 2-auditor [G,H] transfer FS messages. -/
private def tr2aMsgA : ByteArray :=
  transferFsPrefixBytes2A ++ ristrettoBasepointBytes
private def tr2aMsgB : ByteArray :=
  transferFsPrefixBytes2A ++ confidentialAssetHashBaseBytes ++ ristrettoBasepointBytes

/-- 3-auditor [G,H,G] transfer FS messages. -/
private def tr3aMsgA : ByteArray :=
  transferFsPrefixBytes3A ++ ristrettoBasepointBytes
private def tr3aMsgB : ByteArray :=
  transferFsPrefixBytes3A ++ confidentialAssetHashBaseBytes ++ ristrettoBasepointBytes

/-- 2-auditor SWAPPED [H,G] transfer FS messages. -/
private def tr2aSwapMsgA : ByteArray :=
  transferFsPrefixBytes2A_swapped ++ ristrettoBasepointBytes
private def tr2aSwapMsgB : ByteArray :=
  transferFsPrefixBytes2A_swapped ++ confidentialAssetHashBaseBytes ++ ristrettoBasepointBytes

